0	section	Arsen's "curse"
0	section	Talking to Arsen
1	line	Arsen the Thief	Urgh!
1	option	I hear you've been cursed.
2	line	Player	I hear you've been cursed.
2	line	Arsen the Thief	I think so. That navigator, Ithoi, always warned us that this kind of thing could happen.
2	line	Player	I've met him. He definitely thinks it's a curse, but wasn't able to say exactly what caused it.
2	line	Arsen the Thief	I'm afraid it may be all my fault.
2	line	Player	Oh?
2	line	Arsen the Thief	Captain Tock had me exploring some caves, west of the cove. I'm a thief, see, like my brother Francois, and the Captain thought I could sneak past the monsters without being noticed.
2	line	Arsen the Thief	Well, I climbed down the vines, and found a big cave filled with terrifying ogres!
2	line	Arsen the Thief	I'd hoped I could use my amazing Thieving skills to avoid them seeing me, but I was out of luck. By the time I'd finished clambering down the ladder, they'd spotted me.
2	line	Player	So you were trying to explore that ogre cave, and the ogres saw you?
2	line	Arsen the Thief	Yes. I quickly grabbed some loot, so I wouldn't have to face the Captain empty-handed, and fled up the ladder before the ogres could kill me!
2	line	Arsen the Thief	But a couple of days later we all fell ill. I think what I stole must have been some kind of sacred relic, and the shamans in the cave have cursed us for stealing it.
2	line	Arsen the Thief	Maybe you could get the relic back from the Captain, and return it to the ogres? And tell them I'm very sorry. Then perhaps they'll lift the curse.
2	line	Player	I see.
2	action	end
1	option	Urgh to you too, with candy sprinkles on.
2	line	Player	Urgh to you too, with candy sprinkles on.
2	line	Arsen the Thief	A sympathetic soul you are. I'm in real pain here.
2	line	Player	Yes, I hear you've been cursed.
2	action	above
