0	section	Traitor in the midst
0	section	Talking to Captain Tock
1	line	Captain Tock	Have ye any idea about how to lift the curse?
1	option	I've ruled out all the Corsairs' theories...
2	line	Player	I've ruled out all the Corsairs' theories...
2	line	Player	Cabin-boy Colin thought he'd upset a mermaid, but there wasn't a mermaid, just a wet ogre.
2	line	Player	Arsen the Thief thought he'd upset the ogre shamans by stealing a sacred ogre relic, but it was just a tooth-pick, and the ogres didn't care.
2	line	Player	Ithoi the Navigator said there were lots of things that could bring a curse on a crew, and this could be any of them.
2	line	Player	And Gnocci the Cook thought he'd awoken a demon in a possessed doll, but it wasn't possessed at all. It was clockwork.
2	line	Captain Tock	Arrr, any sufficiently advanced technology be indistinguishable from demonic possession, that it be.
2	option	So what do I do now?
3	line	Player	So what do I do now?
3	line	Captain Tock	Arrr, I don't rightly know. It began when I'd gone away for a parlay with Ithoi; we came back ter find the crew all a-pukin' up their dinner. Then Ithoi felt ill too, though he'd not eaten with 'em, so it can't be the food.
3	line	Player	I see. You're saying it began after they'd all eaten, but Ithoi felt ill even though he'd not had any of the food.
3	line	Captain Tock	Arrr, that be right.
3	line	Player	That meal must have been interesting...
3	action	end
2	option	Can I give up and go home?
3	line	Player	Can I give up and go home?
3	line	Captain Tock	If ye wants a ride back to Rimmington, I'll take ye there any time, but I do hope ye can help my poor crew.
1	option	Please take me back to Rimmington.
1	option	I'll talk to you later.
